# "Additional end steps don't come with any other additional steps (such as cleanup). Damage marked on permanents won't be
# removed until you actually get to the cleanup step (which will happen after your second end step)" (Y'shtola Rhul's
# ruling; CR 514.2). On turn 3, in Bot1's first end step, Shock deals 2 damage to Bot2's 0/3 Phyrexian Walker. In the
# additional end step Fanatical Firebrand deals it 1 more, and with 3 damage marked it dies. Had the damage been removed
# between the two end steps, the Walker would live.
# Y'shtola Rhul {4}{U}{U}: Legendary Creature — Cat Druid
#   At the beginning of your end step, exile target creature you control, then return it to the battlefield under its owner's control. Then if it's the first end step of the turn, there is an additional end step after this step.

